Perform a release-candidate end-to-end smoke test of the current ingestion pipeline on `codex/ingestion-onboarding-integration`.

Do not add new architecture or features.

Select the smallest suitable real approved-source dataset already available to the system and exercise the complete user-facing flow:

`approved source → acquisition → inventory → SourceDescriptor → persisted onboarding → human resolution if required → connector/build → TimeF → TimeNet load/read-back → receipt → records → COMPLETED`

Verify state transitions, persisted job state, receipt contents, record APIs, and frontend behavior.

After successful completion, restart only the ingestion API and worker and verify that the completed ingestion, receipt, and records remain available without reacquisition or rebuilding.

If anything fails, identify the smallest root-cause fix necessary to make the end-to-end flow work. Do not perform unrelated refactors, deployment work, coding-agent integration, worktree isolation, or architectural changes.

Report:

1. &#x20;Dataset/source used&#x20;
2. &#x20;Exact state transitions observed&#x20;
3. &#x20;Human-resolution behavior, if exercised&#x20;
4. &#x20;Final TimeF/load verification&#x20;
5. &#x20;Persistence-after-restart result&#x20;
6. &#x20;Any blocking bugs and minimal fixes&#x20;
7. &#x20;Whether the branch is demo-ready

